{
  "quest.0A6417D3BE825CF9.title": "Brew Safely at Home",
  "quest.0A6417D3BE825CF9.quest_subtitle": "Blaze Rods and Nether Wart now become a new workstation",
  "quest.0A6417D3BE825CF9.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: prepare a permanent brewing place in your Overworld base and learn the process.",
    "",
    "Brewing needs a Brewing Stand, Blaze Powder as fuel, Glass Bottles filled with Water, and an ingredient. The three bottle slots at the bottom are processed together; the ingredient goes at the top.",
    "",
    "Set up the Brewing Stand in a lit, protected room near your storage Chests. Potions need no open flame, and a Brewing Stand cannot start a fire.",
    "",
    "The two Blaze Rods brought safely home are exactly enough to begin: one makes two Blaze Powder, while the other becomes part of the Brewing Stand. Take them and the Nether Wart from storage, but process only one Rod at first.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when the brewing place is chosen and both Blaze Rods are still present.",
  ],
  "task.1B7528E4CF936D0A.title": "Brewing place chosen and 2 Blaze Rods checked",

  "quest.2C8639F5D0A47E1B.title": "Make Blaze Powder",
  "quest.2C8639F5D0A47E1B.quest_subtitle": "One Blaze Rod makes two units for fuel and ingredients",
  "quest.2C8639F5D0A47E1B.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: process exactly one Blaze Rod into two Blaze Powder.",
    "",
    "Place one Blaze Rod in any crafting slot. This shapeless recipe produces two Blaze Powder. Leave the second Rod untouched; it is needed for the Brewing Stand in the next step.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/blaze_powder_recipe.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Blaze Powder has two jobs in a Brewing Stand. Placed on the left, it provides fuel for up to 20 brewing operations. Used at the top as an ingredient, it can turn an Awkward Potion into a Potion of Strength. Do not spend all of it carelessly.",
    "",
    "The automatic task completes when two Blaze Powder are in your inventory at the same time.",
  ],
  "task.3D974A06E1B58F2C.title": "Hold 2 Blaze Powder in your inventory at once",

  "quest.4EA85B17F2C6903D.title": "Build a Brewing Stand",
  "quest.4EA85B17F2C6903D.quest_subtitle": "One Blaze Rod above three suitable stone blocks",
  "quest.4EA85B17F2C6903D.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: craft a Brewing Stand and place it at the prepared location.",
    "",
    "Place the remaining Blaze Rod in the centre slot of the middle row. Fill the bottom row with three suitable stone materials. Three Cobblestone are the simplest safe choice; the recipe also accepts other materials from the same stone recipe group.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/brewing_stand_recipe.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Take the Brewing Stand from the result slot and place it on a solid block with right-click. Open it with right-click as well. The automatic task does not consume the Brewing Stand.",
  ],
  "task.5FB96C2803D7A14E.title": "Hold 1 Brewing Stand",

  "quest.60CA7D3914E8B25F.title": "Make Three Glass Bottles",
  "quest.60CA7D3914E8B25F.quest_subtitle": "Three Glass in a V shape makes three reusable Bottles",
  "quest.60CA7D3914E8B25F.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: craft three Glass Bottles for one complete brewing operation.",
    "",
    "If Glass is missing, smelt Sand in a Furnace. Then place one Glass on the left and right of the middle row and one Glass in the centre of the bottom row. The recipe produces three Glass Bottles.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/glass_bottle_recipe.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "After drinking a normal potion, its empty Glass Bottle remains. Store it beside the Brewing Stand so it can be filled with Water and reused.",
    "",
    "The automatic task completes when three empty Glass Bottles are in your inventory at the same time.",
  ],
  "task.71DB8E4A25F9C360.title": "Hold 3 Glass Bottles in your inventory at once",

  "quest.12EC9F5B360AD471.title": "Fill Three Water Bottles",
  "quest.12EC9F5B360AD471.quest_subtitle": "Right-click a Water source while holding a Glass Bottle",
  "quest.12EC9F5B360AD471.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: fill all three Glass Bottles with Water and place them at the bottom of the Brewing Stand.",
    "",
    "Hold a Glass Bottle and right-click a Water source block. Repeat this for all three Bottles. A filled Cauldron also works but loses part of its Water for each Bottle; a Water source is simpler.",
    "",
    "Water Bottles cannot stack. Open the Brewing Stand and use right-click to distribute one Water Bottle into each of the three lower bottle slots.",
    "",
    "Prepare this step in the Overworld: placed Water evaporates immediately in the Nether. Filled Water Bottles still work there, but remain safely at home for this first lesson.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when all three Water Bottles are in the bottom of the Brewing Stand.",
  ],
  "task.23FDA06C471BE582.title": "3 Water Bottles are in the Brewing Stand",

  "quest.340EB17D582CF693.title": "Brew Awkward Potions",
  "quest.340EB17D582CF693.quest_subtitle": "Blaze Powder powers the Stand; Nether Wart creates the foundation",
  "quest.340EB17D582CF693.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: turn the three Water Bottles into Awkward Potions with one Nether Wart.",
    "",
    "Place one Blaze Powder in the square fuel slot at the upper left. The item is consumed immediately; the horizontal field above the left bottle turns yellow instead. It stores 20 charges, one of which is used for each completed brewing operation.",
    "",
    "Put one Nether Wart into the single ingredient slot at the top. When fuel, an ingredient, and at least one suitable bottle are present, the progress bar begins. Wait until it finishes.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/awkward_potion_brewing.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "The three Water Bottles are now called Awkward Potions. They have no effect by themselves, but form the foundation for nearly every useful potion. Leave them in place for now.",
    "",
    "The first completed brewing operation is detected automatically through the Vanilla advancement.",
  ],
  "task.451FC28E693D07A4.title": "Complete a brewing operation for the first time",

  "quest.5620D39F7A4E18B5.title": "Brew Your First Potion of Strength",
  "quest.5620D39F7A4E18B5.quest_subtitle": "Blaze Powder as an ingredient turns Awkward Potions into Strength",
  "quest.5620D39F7A4E18B5.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: turn the three Awkward Potions into Potions of Strength and drink one in a safe place.",
    "",
    "Leave the Awkward Potions at the bottom. The fuel remains on the left; now place another Blaze Powder in the top ingredient slot. Brewing produces three Potions of Strength that last three minutes.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/strength_potion_brewing.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Hold a Potion of Strength and hold right-click to drink it. Strength raises the damage of your melee attacks, but does not protect against fire or falls and does not replace Armour, a Shield, or cover.",
    "",
    "The reward provides three Redstone Dust. Brewing one Redstone Dust into normal Potions of Strength later extends them to eight minutes. Glowstone Dust instead makes stronger but shorter Strength II Potions; both changes cannot be applied to the same Potion.",
    "",
    "A Potion of Fire Resistance is made later from an Awkward Potion and Magma Cream. It is especially helpful on later Nether trips but is not required here.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark only after the Potion of Strength is complete and you have seen its effect icon and remaining time in your inventory.",
    "",
    "Reward: three Redstone Dust allow the first extension, and ten experience points mark your complete first brewing sequence.",
  ],
  "task.6731E4A08B5F29C6.title": "I brewed and drank Strength and checked the effect",

  "quest.1D9468F4A713C5E0.title": "Fire Resistance Is Optional",
  "quest.1D9468F4A713C5E0.quest_subtitle": "A useful Nether potion, but not an invitation to jump into Lava",
  "quest.1D9468F4A713C5E0.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: consciously decide whether to begin the optional Fire Resistance branch now.",
    "",
    "Fire Resistance prevents damage from fire, Lava, Magma Blocks, and Blaze fire attacks while it lasts. This makes it a powerful extra safeguard for later Nether trips.",
    "",
    "The Potion does not protect against melee attacks, arrows, explosions, falls, suffocation, or falling into the Void. It replaces neither Armour and a Shield nor solid cover and a marked retreat.",
    "",
    "This Potion needs Magma Cream. Obtaining it may require another Nether trip or a Slimeball and additional Blaze Powder. The entire branch therefore remains optional and blocks no later main quest.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when you understand its benefit and limits and voluntarily want to begin obtaining the ingredient.",
  ],
  "task.2EA57905B824D6F1.title": "I know the benefit, limits, and optional nature",

  "quest.3FB68A16C935E702.title": "Obtain One Magma Cream",
  "quest.3FB68A16C935E702.quest_subtitle": "Craft it from a Slimeball and Blaze Powder or loot it carefully",
  "quest.3FB68A16C935E702.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: hold one Magma Cream without forcing an unprepared trip.",
    "",
    "The controlled crafting route is shapeless: place one Slimeball and one Blaze Powder in any crafting slots. You may first need to retrieve another Blaze Rod from the already secured Nether Fortress and process it into Powder.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/magma_cream_recipe.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Alternatively, medium and large Magma Cubes can drop Magma Cream; small ones cannot, and a larger Cube does not guarantee a drop. Do not make an unprepared search for one particular Nether biome.",
    "",
    "Fight a Magma Cube only on broad solid ground from a closed retreat room. It splits into smaller Cubes when defeated. Keep the exit blockable and attack each Cube separately with fully charged strikes.",
    "",
    "The automatic task completes when one Magma Cream is in your inventory. Its source does not matter.",
  ],
  "task.40C79B27DA46F813.title": "Hold 1 Magma Cream",

  "quest.51D8AC38EB570924.title": "Brew Fire Resistance",
  "quest.51D8AC38EB570924.quest_subtitle": "Magma Cream turns Awkward Potions into three minutes of protection",
  "quest.51D8AC38EB570924.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: brew up to three Potions of Fire Resistance with a duration of three minutes.",
    "",
    "Fill up to three Glass Bottles with Water and first brew them with Nether Wart into Awkward Potions. Your Brewing Stand's yellow fuel bar should still hold charges; if it does not, load new Blaze Powder into the upper-left slot.",
    "",
    "Leave the Awkward Potions at the bottom and put one Magma Cream into the ingredient slot at the upper centre. After one operation, every inserted bottle becomes a three-minute Potion of Fire Resistance at the same time.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/fire_resistance_brewing.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Do not take the Potions into Lava merely to test them. Store at least one beside the Brewing Stand and set the checkmark after verifying its name and three-minute duration in the inventory.",
  ],
  "task.62E9BD49FC681A35.title": "I brewed Fire Resistance and checked 3:00",

  "quest.73FACD5A0D792B46.title": "Extend Fire Resistance",
  "quest.73FACD5A0D792B46.quest_subtitle": "Redstone changes three minutes into eight, but adds no protection strength",
  "quest.73FACD5A0D792B46.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: extend your Potions of Fire Resistance to eight minutes with one Redstone Dust.",
    "",
    "Leave the ordinary Potions of Fire Resistance at the bottom of the Brewing Stand and place one Redstone Dust at the top as the ingredient. After brewing, the Bottles show Fire Resistance with a duration of eight minutes.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/long_fire_resistance_brewing.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Redstone extends only the duration; Fire Resistance has no stronger Glowstone tier. Drink the Potion immediately before a prepared Nether trip and watch its effect icon and timer. Milk removes the effect immediately.",
    "",
    "Do not test the Potion by deliberately jumping into Lava. It is a reserve for mistakes, not a new way to travel. If you fall in accidentally, stay calm, swim to the nearest solid edge, and leave the Nether before the timer ends.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after at least one Potion shows eight minutes and is stored safely with your travel equipment.",
    "",
    "Reward: five experience points mark this optional safety upgrade.",
  ],
  "task.04ABDE6B1E8A3C57.title": "At least 1 Fire Resistance Potion shows 8:00 and is stored",
}
